# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

Thank you for considering a contribution. Please keep changes focused and explain the problem they solve.

## Welcome

Be respectful, constructive, and welcoming. See [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).

## Ways to contribute

Report reproducible bugs, suggest improvements, improve documentation, add tests, or submit code changes.

## Development setup

1. Fork the repository and clone your fork.
2. Install the project's documented prerequisites and development dependencies.
3. Create a focused feature branch.

## Running tests

Run the test suite and all project quality checks before submitting changes. Document commands and relevant environment requirements here.

## Code style

Follow the existing conventions, keep functions focused, and add tests for behavior changes.

## Pull-request process

Describe the change, link related issues, list validation performed, and call out compatibility or security implications. Do not include secrets or unrelated changes.

## Code of Conduct

Participation is governed by [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).
